{
  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (pca_n2000: 0.485, scvi_n200: 0.520) substantially outperform image-only models (resnet50: 0.208, ViT-L: 0.227), establishing RNA as the dominant signal. However, image performance is only slightly above chance, leaving genuine uncertainty about whether image features provide complementary information in a fused setting or merely add noise. Question tested: Does combining the best RNA encoder (scvi_n200) with the best image encoder (ViT-L) via simple concatenation in a singleprofile setting yield any gain over the RNA-only baseline of 0.520? This is the cleanest multimodal test—singleprofile minimizes confounding variables, and concat is the simplest fusion. Why best next experiment: Resolving whether multimodal fusion is viable at all is the highest-leverage structural decision. A positive result validates ~36 multimodal configurations for further exploration; a null or negative result efficiently prunes that entire branch, redirecting budget toward RNA-only multiprofile/aggregation and encoder choices where the signal clearly resides."
}

